static void Main(string[] args)
{
    int a = 22;
    long b = 44;
    double c = 1.406;
    b = a;
    c = a;
    a = b;
    b = c;
}

questions.explanation:
Conversion of data type from 'int' to 'double' is implicit in nature for 'c = a' as int is subset of double but same is not applicable for 'b = c' as 'c' had wider scope of data range then 'b' so explicit conversion is needed.

 Output :

 Error 1: Can not implicitly convert type 'long' to 'int'. An explicit conversion exists (are you missing a cast?).
 Error 2: Cannot implicitly convert type 'double' to 'long'. An explicit conversion exists (are you missing a cast?).

 Correct solution :

 static void Main(string[] args)
 {
     int a = 22;
     long b = 44;
     double c = 1.406;
     b = a;
     c = a;
     a = (int)b;
     b = (long)c;
 }
